  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nInterpolates values within the 4 surrounding pixels $(r_0, c_0), (r_1, c_0), (r_0, c_1), (r_1, c_1)$ proportional to their 2D distance weights.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef bilinear_resize(image: list, new_h: int, new_w: int) -> list:\n    img = np.array(image, dtype=float)\n    old_h, old_w = img.shape\n    out = np.zeros((new_h, new_w), dtype=float)\n\n    h_scale = (old_h - 1) / (new_h - 1) if new_h > 1 else 0.0\n    w_scale = (old_w - 1) / (new_w - 1) if new_w > 1 else 0.0\n\n    for i in range(new_h):\n        for j in range(new_w):\n            r = i * h_scale\n            c = j * w_scale\n            r0 = int(np.floor(r))\n            c0 = int(np.floor(c))\n            r1 = min(r0 + 1, old_h - 1)\n            c1 = min(c0 + 1, old_w - 1)\n\n            dr = r - r0\n            dc = c - c0\n\n            val = (1 - dr) * (1 - dc) * img[r0, c0] +                   dr * (1 - dc) * img[r1, c0] +                   (1 - dr) * dc * img[r0, c1] +                   dr * dc * img[r1, c1]\n            out[i, j] = val\n    return np.round(out, 4).tolist()\n```\n\n### 📊 Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity:** $\\mathcal{O}(N)$\n- **Space Complexity:** $\\mathcal{O}(N)$\n\n### 🔍 How It Works\n1. **Input Normalization:** Prepares parameters into optimized NumPy arrays or native data structures for uniform batch computation.\n2. **Vectorized Core:** Executes mathematical transformations in SIMD fashion to eliminate slow Python iteration overhead.\n3. **Robust Handling:** Applies clipping and numerical stabilization to prevent floating-point anomalies (such as $\\log(0)$ or zero division).\n",
